WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.165
This is STE-80. It is a writing style for technical text.

2
00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:08.860
It uses most of the rules of ASD-STE100.

3
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.422
Here is a typical sentence from a manual. It has sixteen words.

4
00:00:13.522 --> 00:00:15.746
Some of the words do not help the reader.

5
00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:19.189
Rule one. Use simple words. Replenished becomes full.

6
00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:22.635
Prior to becomes before. Commencing becomes starting.

7
00:00:22.735 --> 00:00:26.535
The length does not change. But each word is easier to read.

8
00:00:27.128 --> 00:00:29.458
Rule two. Give the instruction directly.

9
00:00:29.558 --> 00:00:33.348
Remove the frame around the instruction, and talk to the reader.

10
00:00:33.448 --> 00:00:35.536
The sentence now has thirteen words.

11
00:00:36.128 --> 00:00:38.155
Rule three. Use a concrete verb.

12
00:00:38.255 --> 00:00:41.412
The words make sure and is full describe a state.

13
00:00:41.512 --> 00:00:45.267
The verb fill names the action. Operation becomes machine.

14
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.394
The sentence now has nine words.

15
00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:51.509
Sixteen words became nine. The instruction did not change.

16
00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:53.130
The reader does less work.
